	('2025-06-26 00:43:36.324324+00', 'Roadmap', 'Add Features Log. Add a button to the top right by the bell called “Request Feature” This could be a google form or document if its possible but it could also be a fully coded page. It should allow users to create a new feature request, label them as a feature or a bug, track who submitted the request. Then if they get approved we can see the actual roadmap and update the roadmap whenever.', '3598b33a-fe3e-47b9-bbf8-ca649534d20f', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', 'feature', 'complete'),
	('2025-06-26 00:46:24.468119+00', 'Bleacher Location', 'Beside the bleacher number, put the city(first) and province/state(second). Also add an address field to the teardown and white space block so the bleacher location can use it. The bleacher location logic should be to find today and look left to find the last address. This is where the bleacher should be. If it''s currently in an event, then use this address.', 'f7651b95-bad6-489f-8799-3d2602a8bb43', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', 'feature', 'complete'),
	('2025-06-26 00:45:33.918833+00', 'Bleacher Colours', 'Bring back the coloured labels for bleacher dashboard', '1aa4b481-b220-44b0-a9ea-6633efabf89f', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', 'feature', 'complete'),
	('2025-06-26 00:44:44.196943+00', 'Remove Home Base Rule', 'Remove Rule stating events must be within a home base.

NOTE FROM JOSH:
If you''re an admin, you can create any event, anywhere. If you''re an Account Manager you can only create/edit/delete events within your home base. I know this will need to be changed in the future but since we''re all admins it seems like the most logical way to go.', '05b1ff21-74e5-480a-a06d-626957226cf8', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', 'feature', 'complete'),
	('2025-06-26 00:45:55.472515+00', 'Event Link Field', 'Add link field to event details. If there is a link in the url field, display a good shuffle logo beside the Event Name and make it clickable. When you click the link it opens the good shuffle page in a new tab.', 'adef5868-f514-4dcf-a57c-a580c46063c5', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', 'feature', 'complete'),
	('2025-06-26 00:46:11.341863+00', 'Scroll to top', 'When you select an event, scroll to the top of the dashboard so you can see the selected bleachers.', 'b4dfb833-aa3f-4b79-a5fe-2eb713cc31ce', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', 'feature', 'complete'),
	('2025-06-27 18:49:06.661234+00', 'sorting by event location', 'events under Y axis should be able to sort by province and state,    Make this a multi select.

Here is a demo: https://www.loom.com/share/36399ffc1c4a4f5da9299bf511843708?sid=e1e62544-a2bd-4910-b3ba-8dcda8f89143', 'c24074f6-392d-4af9-bb65-7494e88ac500', '6b080032-c889-4ce5-86e0-5a564a4d97f7', 'feature', 'complete'),
	('2025-06-27 18:53:16.543143+00', 'add driver', 'add user type,  driver,    add or invite possible. Don''t send invite email just add to database', '78ee8ead-878a-4f2e-b9d1-44d31b2519bd', '6b080032-c889-4ce5-86e0-5a564a4d97f7', 'feature', 'complete'),
	('2025-06-26 18:53:58.541255+00', 'Update Cell Click Outside the modal', 'When I edit a cell in the dashboard I try to copy all the text by highlighting the text with the mouse but a lot of the time I release the mouse button outside the popup and this closes it. Can you change this functionality to maybe only close the pop up with the mouse button was pressed and released outside the modal to ensure that it was closed intentionally?', 'e988f01f-ffc6-4bd5-99e8-2db273bd3b12', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', 'feature', 'complete'),
	('2025-08-01 14:17:05.483578+00', 'Tax to work tracker', 'under driver assign tax percent (optional)', 'cd500fad-c783-472f-8a20-8beb5b6aa118', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', 'feature', 'complete'),
	('2025-06-27 20:09:50.380504+00', 'Work Trackers', 'Setup Block should have
Select a driver from a drop down list
Should have a toggle for selecting a primary driver. If there is already another primary driver then it should display a popup saying are you sure you want to change primary driver from [Name] to [New Name]?
Cannot change drop off address and you don’t even need to see it.
Pickup address can be the bleachers last event, the bleachers home base, or an arbitrary address.
Both P/O & D/O POC should be just a text field for now.
DATE: Should this be selectable within the setup range?-doesn’t look like it. Default to the first date in the setup range?
TIME: a lot of the time you put morning, any, or you’ll put a specific time. How would you want to handle this? JUST A TEXT FIELD.
EXTERNAL NOTES ( VISIBLE TO THE DRIVER ON WORK TRACKER)
Should still be able to just type in text while this feature is in its infancy. Maybe we could put an icon on it if it has a work tracker configured?
The block on the dashboard should always be populated with the driver name first and then any additional INTERNAL/DASHBOARD notes that the AM wrote. These notes should not be visible to the driver on the work tracker just on the dashboard.


If an address is specified in a teardown or a regular block this should be considered when calculating todays location for this bleacher.


Event Details POC fields should be
Just Name and Phone fields.

Work trackers page
Allow for fully manual input.
Export to xlsx
Should be able to click on a row and edit it like you clicked on a setup/teardown block. These edits should change on the dashboard too.

Just make sure everything is editable and then download as PDF.
', '44e2730c-9267-45eb-8543-ffb13c277e7b', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', 'feature', 'complete'),
	('2025-07-02 17:38:49.421378+00', 'Laggy when typing', 'Sometimes it''s laggy when typing on a block. Look into it', '25be8abb-1b64-4093-a9ba-298fb37edbe4', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', 'bug', 'complete');


